# Privacy Policy of Gumshark
## Information and relevant links

> [GitHub](https://github.com/PxINKY)

Gumshark is a public, privately owned Discord bot [Python 3.10](https://www.python.org/) + [Discord.py](https://discordpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) + [Gumroad API](https://gumroad.com/api) to create an API bridge for Gumroad and Discord. Allowing users to connect online purchases with in-server channels

Gumshark was created by me (PxINKY); it started out as a passion project and evolved into a public bot that can be used in public/private Discord servers.


### 1. Using Gumshark
a. Gumshark has permission to collect the following information:

* Guild name and ID

* Guild user count

* User commands/messages

* Gumroad purchase license IDs


### 2. Why this information?
a. Guild name / ID

* The use of collecting Guild names and IDs allows me to log the total number of servers that Gumshark is in.

* This is used in the splash tag/descriptor on the bot's active status

* Also, if the TOS of Gumshark is broken, this allows me to blacklist servers


b. Guild user count

* Allows for future implementations such as guild user count


c. User commands/messages

* Without the ability to read the message, Gumshark wouldn't be able to tell when receiving a command. As it allows the use of legacy commands in combination with slash commands


d. Gumroad purchase license IDs

* These are collected and stored alongside User IDs to link purchases to the Discord account. This prevents issues when a user changes their username. Additionally, this is logged for back-end reasons to make sure purchases aren't authenticated on multiple accounts.

